1
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:48,009
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:51,050
[Episode 8]

3
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:52,750
[Steal A Moment To Sip Wine Guesthouse]

4
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:46,079
My head hurts.

5
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:50,010
How did I get back here?

6
00:03:26,079 --> 00:03:27,079
Gosh, Yun Li,

7
00:03:27,079 --> 00:03:29,360
what did you do?

8
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:33,240
Does your head still hurt?

9
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,460
W-Why are you here?

10
00:03:43,750 --> 00:03:45,079
It was too late to leave.

11
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:49,500
Y-You get some rest then.

12
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,160
I-I'm heading back to my room.

13
00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:15,470
This is odd.

14
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:17,680
Doesn't she usually jog here?

15
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:24,720
Why is he still here?

16
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:27,170
Why did I have to drink so much?

17
00:04:27,170 --> 00:04:28,300
Now this is awkward.

18
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,159
Morning, Xia.

19
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:43,659
Morning.

20
00:04:43,659 --> 00:04:44,190
Morning.

21
00:04:48,110 --> 00:04:49,480
Did he just greet us?

22
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,040
I think so.

23
00:04:52,450 --> 00:04:54,510
The sun must have risen from the west.

24
00:05:03,450 --> 00:05:04,250
It's okay.

25
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:06,220
I won't run into him as long as I stay

26
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:07,420
away from the Engineering.

27
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:08,160
Yun Li!

28
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:10,220
I was just looking for you.

29
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,550
We're running a test
on the Light Chaser today.

30
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:13,010
You should go and help out.

31
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:15,010
Are you busy?

32
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:15,770
No.

33
00:05:15,770 --> 00:05:17,010
I-I...

34
00:05:17,070 --> 00:05:17,870
Yun Li,

35
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:19,030
are you very busy?

36
00:05:19,030 --> 00:05:20,230
I can go in your stead.

37
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,680
No, I'll go.

38
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,910
Then you stay and organize the materials.

39
00:05:30,910 --> 00:05:32,110
I'll let you know if I need anything.

40
00:05:32,110 --> 00:05:33,120
Okay, Ms. Fang.

41
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:38,920
Mr. Qin!

42
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:39,920
Good morning.

43
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,180
How about some coffee?

44
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,470
Sure, a cup for me.

45
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:45,980
Yun Li,

46
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:47,620
why did you have to say yes?

47
00:05:49,630 --> 00:05:50,330
What if

48
00:05:50,330 --> 00:05:51,430
you run into Fu Shize later?

49
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:52,690
Won't that be awkward?

50
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:59,240
Welcome to the Light Chaser.

51
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:02,350
You are about to embark on
a journey of wonders.

52
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,250
I'm sorry about last night.

53
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:13,360
I shouldn't have drunk so much alcohol.

54
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,450
I might have said something,

55
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:17,000
but I didn't mean it.

56
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:19,480
You...

57
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,120
Just pretend nothing happened.

58
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:21,800
Don't ask, either.

59
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,660
I really have no idea whatsoever.

60
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:29,310
Are you...

61
00:06:31,810 --> 00:06:33,100
here to help out?

62
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:37,120
What do I need to do?

63
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:41,860
Mr. Qin.

64
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,860
Here's your double Americano,
extra strong.

65
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:44,659
Thank you.

66
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:49,159
Really, the coffee you make suits

67
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,620
my taste the best, Feifei.

68
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:52,300
Mr. Qin,

69
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,159
how well do you know

70
00:06:54,310 --> 00:06:55,310
Engineer Fu?

71
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:56,190
Engineer Fu?

72
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:57,450
He's just an engineer

73
00:06:57,450 --> 00:06:58,220
in the engineering department.

74
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,750
We don't interact much at work.

75
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:00,880
I'm not close to him.

76
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:05,320
But it seems to me that Mr. Xu has quite

77
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:07,200
an unusual tie with him.

78
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,290
You do have a keen eye.

79
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:11,980
Listen,

80
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:14,790
they are actually relatives.

81
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:18,730
Relatives?

82
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:19,680
Yes.

83
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,560
Didn't expect that, huh?

84
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,800
How do I tie this?

85
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:35,860
Let me help.

86
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,450
When the machine's officially
open to the public,

87
00:07:53,450 --> 00:07:54,600
will there be staff

88
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,560
to assist?

89
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:56,370
Yes.

90
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,330
Is it too tight?

91
00:08:04,890 --> 00:08:05,690
No, it's not.

92
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,800
The player's heart rate is spiking.

93
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:13,880
There's even a heart rate monitor?

94
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:16,000
Any player who feels unwell will be

95
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,130
automatically removed from the game.

96
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:22,890
Are you...

97
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:24,930
nervous?

98
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,330
To be more accurate,

99
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,490
I am utterly nervous.

100
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,150
I'll be with you for the first experience

101
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:35,460
and collect the data separately later.

102
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,460
Then you won't be nervous.

103
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:05,550
He looks so handsome

104
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,740
in this suit.

105
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:10,170
Alert. Alert.

106
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,440
Player One has

107
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:14,370
a rapid heart rate
and an elevated body temperature.

108
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,150
Yun Li, compose yourself.

109
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,430
Newton's First Law says

110
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,220
that every object persists in its state

111
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:26,630
of rest or uniform motion
in a straight line

112
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:30,680
unless it's compelled to change
that state by an external force.

113
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:36,500
Are you ready?

114
00:09:41,170 --> 00:09:42,030
Yes, I'm ready.

115
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:53,250
Where would you like to go?

116
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:59,240
The moon. Is it okay?

117
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:01,270
You want to land on the moon?

118
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:02,080
Yes.

119
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:04,390
Very much so.

120
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:10,030
You have chosen
the moon landing experience.

121
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:10,890
It's starting.

122
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:14,480
Program loading is completed.

123
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:15,980
Ready for departure.

124
00:10:25,590 --> 00:10:27,540
♪ If sometimes ♪

125
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:31,370
♪ You feel discouraged ♪

126
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:34,630
♪ I'll be behind you ♪

127
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:37,950
♪ And keep all the rainstorms from you ♪

128
00:10:40,170 --> 00:10:42,360
♪ I don't need anyone to prove ♪

129
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:46,190
♪ Whether I win in this adventure ♪

130
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,760
♪ Let me draw near again ♪

131
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:53,500
♪ Every little bit of your heart ♪

132
00:10:55,410 --> 00:10:58,890
♪ I know those fears ♪

133
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:03,220
♪ May never truly fade away ♪

134
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:06,270
♪ But I still believe ♪

135
00:11:06,310 --> 00:11:09,000
♪ That we'll meet someday ♪

136
00:11:11,430 --> 00:11:13,010
♪ It's you ♪

137
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:15,340
♪ Even with my eyes closed ♪

138
00:11:15,370 --> 00:11:16,890
♪ Just you ♪

139
00:11:16,910 --> 00:11:19,280
♪ Feel so right to my heart ♪

140
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:20,690
♪ This moon tonight ♪

141
00:11:20,710 --> 00:11:22,940
♪ Brings faded colors back to life ♪

142
00:11:22,970 --> 00:11:26,270
♪ And keeps me company through
the endless night ♪

143
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:26,410
Come here.

144
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,390
♪ It's you ♪

145
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:30,580
♪ Even if I forget everything ♪

146
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:31,890
♪ Just you ♪

147
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:34,260
♪ Can fill the emptiness in my heart ♪

148
00:11:34,390 --> 00:11:35,800
♪ By your side ♪

149
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:36,810
♪ Even the most ordinary seasons ♪

150
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,190
♪ Feel warm again ♪

151
00:11:40,230 --> 00:11:43,290
♪ It's you ♪

152
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:00,890
♪ It's you ♪

153
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:03,220
♪ Even with my eyes closed ♪

154
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,760
♪ Just you ♪

155
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:07,150
♪ Feel so right to my heart ♪

156
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:08,560
♪ This moon tonight ♪

157
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,820
♪ Brings faded colors back to life ♪

158
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:14,150
♪ And keeps me company through
the endless night ♪

159
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:14,890
Alert! Alert!

160
00:12:14,590 --> 00:12:16,260
♪ It's you ♪

161
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:16,120
Player One's heart rate

162
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:16,820
is spiking.

163
00:12:16,290 --> 00:12:18,450
♪ Even if I forget everything ♪

164
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:17,550
I'm not nervous.

165
00:12:17,550 --> 00:12:18,720
I don't want to quit the game now.

166
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:19,510
♪ Just you ♪

167
00:12:19,370 --> 00:12:20,500
Newton's Second Law says

168
00:12:19,790 --> 00:12:22,130
♪ Can fill the emptiness in my heart ♪

169
00:12:21,370 --> 00:12:23,100
that a force causes an object
to accelerate.

170
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,680
♪ By your side ♪

171
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,700
The acceleration is directly proportional
to the net force

172
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,680
♪ Even the most ordinary seasons ♪

173
00:12:24,710 --> 00:12:27,060
♪ Feel warm again ♪

174
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:28,110
and inversely proportional
to the mass of the object.

175
00:12:28,110 --> 00:12:30,510
♪ It's you ♪

176
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:30,670
The direction of the acceleration

177
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:33,130
is the same as the direction
of the net force.

178
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,620
Alert! Alert!

179
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:36,550
The player's heart rate is too high.

180
00:12:36,550 --> 00:12:38,880
The game is shutting down automatically.

181
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,320
I'm sorry.

182
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:02,340
Alert! Alert!

183
00:13:02,770 --> 00:13:04,770
Player Two's heart rate is spiking.

184
00:13:18,390 --> 00:13:19,180
Yun Li.

185
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:23,910
Why is your face so red?

186
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:27,880
It's really hot today.

187
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:31,050
Feifei! Come with me.

188
00:13:40,650 --> 00:13:41,600
Just now,

189
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:42,700
Mr. Xu posted a notice

190
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:43,460
in the leaders' chat group.

191
00:13:43,460 --> 00:13:44,740
Starting tomorrow,

192
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:45,960
all departments in the company

193
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,200
must fully cooperate with

194
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,340
the publicity campaign
for the Light Chaser.

195
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:49,890
Tomorrow, there will be an announcement

196
00:13:49,890 --> 00:13:51,700
about launching a company-wide
pitch competition

197
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:52,530
for this campaign.

198
00:13:52,530 --> 00:13:53,340
I haven't told

199
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,600
the news to anyone else yet.

200
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:55,960
Think about it and get

201
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,090
prepared, will you?

202
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:58,800
Thank you, Mr. Qin.

203
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:15,550
Miss?

204
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:18,600
You gave me such a fright.

205
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:21,600
You don't work
in the engineering department, do you?

206
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,000
No, I don't.

207
00:14:23,710 --> 00:14:25,570
I'm here to meet with Engineer Fu.

208
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,000
Shall I go get him for you?

209
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:29,550
No, no need.

210
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:34,550
You are...

211
00:14:35,410 --> 00:14:36,670
M-My surname is Xia.

212
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:38,890
Hello.

213
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:42,460
Fu Shize is an engineer here, right?

214
00:14:42,650 --> 00:14:44,050
He's the chief engineer.

215
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:49,140
So the Light Chaser...

216
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,600
It's exactly his design.

217
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:01,480
I shouldn't have drunk alcohol.

218
00:15:04,870 --> 00:15:07,120
Alcohol is no good.

219
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:12,590
Why are you also in distress?

220
00:15:13,890 --> 00:15:15,940
Did you also drink too much last night?

221
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:17,140
Don't get me started.

222
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:18,500
I didn't even know

223
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:19,370
how I got back.

224
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,480
Then what do you remember?

225
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,670
I only remember I had too much to drink.

226
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,390
Fu Zhengchu came help me,

227
00:15:26,390 --> 00:15:28,130
and then we talked a lot.

228
00:15:30,630 --> 00:15:31,630
Fu Zhengchu.

229
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:36,130
I like you.

230
00:15:39,910 --> 00:15:40,370
I...

231
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:46,080
I think I told him I like him.

232
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:47,870
And...

233
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:50,990
I even kissed him.

234
00:15:56,370 --> 00:15:57,170
No way.

235
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:58,670
You kissed him?

236
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:00,790
I'm not sure

237
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,130
if I kissed him or not.

238
00:16:03,110 --> 00:16:04,170
I only remember...

239
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:07,670
that I grabbed his collar like this,

240
00:16:08,790 --> 00:16:11,390
and leaned in.

241
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:14,430
As for the rest, I don't recall.

242
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,600
Suppose I did kiss him,
I didn't feel anything.

243
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,330
So let's say it never happened.

244
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:25,840
Lili,

245
00:16:26,050 --> 00:16:26,980
what's with you?

246
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:29,960
So you're just dwelling on

247
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:32,220
whether you kissed him or not?

248
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,410
Of course not.

249
00:16:35,220 --> 00:16:36,750
Whether I kissed him or not,

250
00:16:37,010 --> 00:16:38,320
won't it be awkward

251
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,920
when we see each other again?

252
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:42,000
When I went jogging today,

253
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,550
he was standing there waiting for me.

254
00:16:43,550 --> 00:16:46,210
I was so scared
that I turned around and ran away.

255
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:48,050
I'm too ashamed to see him now.

256
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:50,010
Tangy,

257
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,560
I also have something to tell you.

258
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:54,010
What is it?

259
00:16:55,210 --> 00:16:58,070
It's unclear whether you kissed
Fu Zhengchu or not,

260
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:01,070
but I think I did kiss Fu Shize.

261
00:17:05,109 --> 00:17:06,170
When did it happen?

262
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:09,050
Yesterday, when he brought me back here.

263
00:17:09,050 --> 00:17:10,420
A little accident happened,

264
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:11,220
and then we...

265
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,160
Did Fu Shize lose control after drinking?

266
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:15,920
No, no, no.

267
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,650
It was really just an accident.

268
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:21,290
Did you see him today?

269
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:22,310
What did he say?

270
00:17:23,810 --> 00:17:25,109
I made up my mind

271
00:17:25,109 --> 00:17:26,700
to avoid him,

272
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:28,050
but the more I tried to do so,

273
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:29,650
the more often I ran into him.

274
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:32,350
I was assigned to help with
testing the Light Chaser.

275
00:17:32,350 --> 00:17:33,110
And then?

276
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:34,550
Then, during the test,

277
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,110
he and I were very close.

278
00:17:36,110 --> 00:17:37,770
I just looked at him like this.

279
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:40,000
The heart rate monitor

280
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,090
kept raising the alarm.

281
00:17:42,290 --> 00:17:43,400
I didn't even dare to look him in the eye.

282
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,050
Do you know how awkward it was?

283
00:17:45,050 --> 00:17:46,610
That's so embarrassing.

284
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:47,720
How is it any different

285
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:48,920
from telling him that you like him?

286
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,850
Who would say "I like you" that way?

287
00:17:51,850 --> 00:17:53,980
Did he ask you to take responsibility?

288
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:55,310
Who cares what he said?

289
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:56,110
Once the game ended,

290
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:57,370
I ran away immediately.

291
00:17:57,370 --> 00:17:58,750
Why did you run?

292
00:17:58,750 --> 00:17:59,900
You already kissed him.

293
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:01,220
You should act now and make him

294
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:02,220
your boyfriend.

295
00:18:03,010 --> 00:18:04,210
What should I do then?

296
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,250
Take the initiative.

297
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,050
Ask him out.

298
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,760
What about you, Ms. Strategist?

299
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:09,880
Me?

300
00:18:10,830 --> 00:18:12,900
I'll wait a couple of days and see.

301
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:13,720
D-Don't.

302
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,290
Tomorrow.

303
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:15,510
Come on, let's go for it tomorrow.

304
00:18:15,510 --> 00:18:18,240
We can overcome anything
when we stand together.

305
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:19,670
Just do it!

306
00:18:20,570 --> 00:18:22,030
Yeah, overcome anything.

307
00:19:13,510 --> 00:19:15,110
G-Good morning.

308
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,500
Morning.

309
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,420
You came quite early today.

310
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:33,090
Do you like coffee a lot?

311
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:33,960
So-so.

312
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:36,460
Could you get me a cup as well?

313
00:19:41,070 --> 00:19:42,800
Didn't you just get some water?

314
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:04,020
A-Anything wrong?

315
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,050
Out of beans.

316
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:12,850
How about you take this cup?

317
00:20:12,850 --> 00:20:13,980
No, no. You drink it.

318
00:20:19,830 --> 00:20:20,960
I'll look for beans.

319
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:31,570
N-No more beans, right?

320
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:33,400
I was just planning
to buy some coffee beans,

321
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,200
but I don't know much about them.

322
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,380
I heard there is a fair today.

323
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,590
There should be

324
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:41,240
many stalls selling coffee beans.

325
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,900
Can you go with me?

326
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,640
If you're not available, I...

327
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:50,330
What time?

328
00:20:51,030 --> 00:20:51,890
Eight o'clock.

329
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:53,290
Okay.

330
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:56,990
I'll get back to work then.

331
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:58,760
See you tonight!

332
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:13,290
Show it to me now!

333
00:21:14,330 --> 00:21:15,140
Well...

334
00:21:15,430 --> 00:21:16,230
You guys go ahead.

335
00:21:16,230 --> 00:21:17,550
I'll be with you in a bit.

336
00:21:17,550 --> 00:21:17,920
Okay.

337
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:18,780
We'll go first.

338
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,240
Fu Zhengchu!

339
00:21:28,570 --> 00:21:29,440
Why run away?

340
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:31,660
Wh-What a coincidence.

341
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,740
I-I was just afraid

342
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:36,610
that you'd feel awkward seeing me.

343
00:21:36,610 --> 00:21:37,920
Who would feel awkward?

344
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:38,720
I would.

345
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,480
Awkward about what?

346
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:41,980
Well, that night...

347
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:42,980
That night...

348
00:21:43,910 --> 00:21:45,060
Nothing happened.

349
00:21:46,030 --> 00:21:46,830
Yes.

350
00:21:47,050 --> 00:21:47,960
Nothing happened.

351
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:48,750
Even if something happened,

352
00:21:48,750 --> 00:21:50,550
let's pretend it didn't.

353
00:21:51,290 --> 00:21:53,090
Is that a tongue twister or what?

354
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:56,790
Take this.

355
00:22:01,750 --> 00:22:03,050
Don't overthink it.

356
00:22:03,050 --> 00:22:03,960
It was free of charge,

357
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,140
so I thought I might as well take it.

358
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:06,940
And as it happens, you love cola.

359
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:08,440
It's yours.

360
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:14,640
Don't you dislike cola?

361
00:22:20,330 --> 00:22:21,460
I like it now.

362
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:25,770
I don't have classes this afternoon.

363
00:22:25,770 --> 00:22:27,500
Shall we have dinner together?

364
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:28,510
Tonight?

365
00:22:28,510 --> 00:22:29,330
I'm afraid I can't,

366
00:22:29,330 --> 00:22:30,260
due to training.

367
00:22:30,740 --> 00:22:31,830
Do you mean you're so busy

368
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:32,570
that you can't eat?

369
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:34,080
I usually don't eat much

370
00:22:34,110 --> 00:22:35,440
when there's training.

371
00:22:38,410 --> 00:22:39,870
I'll head to training now.

372
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,270
Bye.

373
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:51,160
Great news.

374
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,200
I just asked Fu Shize

375
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,240
to buy coffee beans with me,

376
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:54,180
and he said yes.

377
00:22:56,950 --> 00:22:58,620
Good for you, Yun Li.

378
00:22:58,900 --> 00:22:59,570
But are you really

379
00:22:59,570 --> 00:23:00,900
just going to buy beans?

380
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:03,790
R-Really.

381
00:23:03,830 --> 00:23:05,350
Why don't you join us?

382
00:23:05,770 --> 00:23:06,610
No, I won't.

383
00:23:06,810 --> 00:23:08,400
I'd hate to be a third wheel.

384
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,420
It's time I fought for

385
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:12,420
my own happiness.

386
00:23:13,570 --> 00:23:15,010
You've got this, senior!

387
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:17,380
Impressive!

388
00:23:17,590 --> 00:23:18,990
Senior Fu's so handsome.

389
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,750
Cool, Senior Fu!

390
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:27,500
You're so cool, Senior Fu.

391
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:28,500
You look amazing.

392
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:32,240
"Senior Fu, you're so cool."

393
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,200
Senior Fu,

394
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,290
what you did was amazing.

395
00:23:34,290 --> 00:23:35,480
Can you teach me?

396
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,480
Maybe next time.

397
00:23:36,740 --> 00:23:37,680
It's a deal then!

398
00:23:45,530 --> 00:23:46,330
Let's go.

399
00:23:46,510 --> 00:23:47,220
Where to?

400
00:23:48,070 --> 00:23:48,930
To have dinner.

401
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:52,130
Didn't you just refuse?

402
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:53,250
Bravo!

403
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:54,800
I'm hungry now.

404
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,270
Let's go.

405
00:23:58,050 --> 00:23:58,750
Next round!

406
00:24:01,410 --> 00:24:02,200
Come on.

407
00:24:22,310 --> 00:24:23,030
Yun Li!

408
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:48,860
You look great in a trench coat.

409
00:24:54,590 --> 00:24:56,120
And you look great in white.

410
00:25:02,830 --> 00:25:03,640
Let's go.

411
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:24,370
It's over there.

412
00:25:24,550 --> 00:25:25,030
Okay.

413
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:26,500
Take care.

414
00:25:27,580 --> 00:25:28,350
Sir, miss,

415
00:25:28,510 --> 00:25:29,660
looking to buy coffee beans?

416
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:30,880
They were freshly roasted this morning.

417
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:32,010
Feel free to browse.

418
00:25:32,220 --> 00:25:33,570
Any Arabica dark roast beans?

419
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:34,250
Yes.

420
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:35,900
This batch is fresh out of the roaster.

421
00:25:35,900 --> 00:25:36,560
Take a look.

422
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:49,720
I'll take this. Five pounds.

423
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:50,290
Okay.

424
00:25:51,030 --> 00:25:51,570
What else would you like?

425
00:25:51,570 --> 00:25:52,970
Feel free to look around.

426
00:25:55,610 --> 00:25:56,810
Which one do you want?

427
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:58,530
I'd like to smell this one.

428
00:26:08,070 --> 00:26:08,930
Smells so good.

429
00:26:12,380 --> 00:26:14,350
I-I meant the coffee beans.

430
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:17,610
Why not taste it?

431
00:26:23,110 --> 00:26:24,750
It tastes like chocolate.

432
00:26:26,570 --> 00:26:27,770
We'll take this then?

433
00:26:28,270 --> 00:26:28,880
Sir,

434
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,110
I'll take two packs of this.

435
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:30,920
Okay.

436
00:26:31,460 --> 00:26:32,810
Just shop around the place and come back

437
00:26:32,810 --> 00:26:34,010
to pick them up later.

438
00:26:36,810 --> 00:26:38,210
Why did you buy two packs?

439
00:26:38,380 --> 00:26:39,640
I meant to give you one.

440
00:26:41,350 --> 00:26:42,160
No need.

441
00:26:42,380 --> 00:26:43,420
But I insist.

442
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:46,920
You've paid

443
00:26:46,920 --> 00:26:48,160
many times for me.

444
00:26:49,010 --> 00:26:50,850
I feel like I owe you money.

445
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:55,250
If that's the reason,

446
00:26:57,510 --> 00:26:59,040
then let's keep it this way.

447
00:27:03,110 --> 00:27:04,150
Sugar painting!

448
00:27:04,350 --> 00:27:06,150
Traditional craft, take a look!

449
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,020
I want to play that.

450
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:41,300
Take a look.

451
00:27:41,530 --> 00:27:42,050
Sir,

452
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:43,050
I'll just spin this, right?

453
00:27:43,050 --> 00:27:43,380
Yes.

454
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:54,180
Well, the day before yesterday...

455
00:27:56,710 --> 00:27:59,040
Didn't we agree not to
talk about that day?

456
00:27:59,920 --> 00:28:00,750
No.

457
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:02,270
I'm trying to say

458
00:28:02,270 --> 00:28:02,880
if you really

459
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:03,920
can't hold your liquor,

460
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,110
then don't take drinks for me next time.

461
00:28:05,110 --> 00:28:05,480
I...

462
00:28:05,480 --> 00:28:06,680
In fact, I can hold my liquor.

463
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,380
If someone tries to make you drink a lot

464
00:28:08,380 --> 00:28:10,380
next time, turn to me. I'll help you.

465
00:28:10,550 --> 00:28:11,810
There's no next time.

466
00:28:12,380 --> 00:28:14,440
I can't drink anymore or I'll be dead.

467
00:28:19,570 --> 00:28:20,380
Tang Lin.

468
00:28:21,790 --> 00:28:22,680
Are those two

469
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:24,030
Uncle and Lili?

470
00:28:27,740 --> 00:28:28,380
Un...

471
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:29,680
Shut up!

472
00:28:31,090 --> 00:28:32,570
Why are you so clueless?

473
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:34,030
Can't I even say hi?

474
00:28:34,110 --> 00:28:35,330
A man and a woman

475
00:28:35,330 --> 00:28:37,330
are hanging out at a fair
in the middle of the night.

476
00:28:37,330 --> 00:28:39,130
What do you think they're doing?

477
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:43,480
They're on a date?

478
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:44,420
Exactly!

479
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:45,980
They're on a date.

480
00:28:45,980 --> 00:28:47,380
You want to be a third wheel or what?

481
00:28:47,380 --> 00:28:48,180
You're right.

482
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:51,660
I almost... ruined it.

483
00:28:56,180 --> 00:28:57,550
The Pumpkin Man?

484
00:29:01,450 --> 00:29:02,180
Here you go, the Pumpkin Man.

485
00:29:02,180 --> 00:29:02,980
It's so small.

486
00:29:05,510 --> 00:29:06,310
Why don't you take it?

487
00:29:06,310 --> 00:29:07,000
No.

488
00:29:07,350 --> 00:29:08,750
I'll spin it and win a big one for myself.

489
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:09,350
Let me tell you,

490
00:29:09,350 --> 00:29:10,500
I've always won the grand prize every time

491
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:11,810
I spin a wheel like this
since I was little.

492
00:29:11,810 --> 00:29:12,740
Never a slip-up.

493
00:29:15,700 --> 00:29:16,460
See?

494
00:29:16,460 --> 00:29:17,130
I told you so.

495
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:18,730
I always get the grand prize.

496
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:19,510
Sir,

497
00:29:19,530 --> 00:29:20,790
the butterfly one's big, right?

498
00:29:20,790 --> 00:29:21,240
Yes.

499
00:29:48,850 --> 00:29:50,640
Don't you think

500
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:51,640
they're giving off

501
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:53,500
a romantic vibe already?

502
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:15,000
Yun Li?

503
00:30:16,140 --> 00:30:17,730
It really is you.

504
00:30:18,590 --> 00:30:19,750
I stared for a while

505
00:30:19,750 --> 00:30:21,270
but didn't dare to come up.

506
00:30:23,090 --> 00:30:24,830
I never expected to run into you here.

507
00:30:24,830 --> 00:30:26,700
How many years has it been
since we last met?

508
00:30:26,700 --> 00:30:27,960
Don't you remember me?

509
00:30:28,530 --> 00:30:30,000
I'm Qu Mingxin,

510
00:30:30,030 --> 00:30:31,920
your best friend in high school.

511
00:30:33,010 --> 00:30:33,980
I remember you.

512
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:39,530
Is this your boyfriend?

513
00:30:40,540 --> 00:30:42,000
He's very good-looking.

514
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:42,980
He...

515
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:46,490
No.

516
00:30:47,140 --> 00:30:48,560
He's just a co-worker.

517
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:50,900
So you have a job now?

518
00:30:52,270 --> 00:30:53,330
I-I heard you didn't

519
00:30:53,330 --> 00:30:55,160
get recommended for graduate school.

520
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:56,660
You're not planning
to take the entrance exam?

521
00:30:56,660 --> 00:30:57,270
Or...

522
00:30:58,250 --> 00:30:59,590
Did you already fail it?

523
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:03,410
I'm currently a graduate student in Nanwu

524
00:31:03,410 --> 00:31:04,620
and doing an internship.

525
00:31:04,620 --> 00:31:05,430
Really?

526
00:31:05,590 --> 00:31:07,720
That’s great.
Here’s your butterfly.

527
00:31:08,090 --> 00:31:08,900
Thank you.

528
00:31:10,030 --> 00:31:11,700
It's been ages since we last met.

529
00:31:11,700 --> 00:31:13,200
We must have a meal together someday

530
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:14,530
and do some catching up.

531
00:31:15,460 --> 00:31:17,400
Then wait till that someday comes.

532
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:19,020
We're leaving.

533
00:31:19,570 --> 00:31:20,370
Goodbye.

534
00:31:20,700 --> 00:31:21,500
Bye!

535
00:31:27,460 --> 00:31:28,270
Sorry

536
00:31:28,390 --> 00:31:29,720
for taking up your time.

537
00:31:33,490 --> 00:31:34,820
Is she a friend of yours?

538
00:31:35,790 --> 00:31:37,050
Sort of.

539
00:31:37,330 --> 00:31:38,990
I went to high school with her.

540
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,500
At that time,

541
00:31:44,890 --> 00:31:46,370
she tried to isolate me.

542
00:31:47,220 --> 00:31:48,240
I thought we could make

543
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:49,440
really good friends.

544
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:52,550
I don't know how,

545
00:31:53,010 --> 00:31:55,540
but I did get defeated
by something like that.

546
00:31:57,330 --> 00:31:59,240
Perhaps if I had been braver back then,

547
00:31:59,240 --> 00:31:59,920
others wouldn't have

548
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:01,120
shut me out like that.

549
00:32:01,750 --> 00:32:02,530
At the end of the day,

550
00:32:02,530 --> 00:32:03,880
it was all my fault.

551
00:32:06,290 --> 00:32:08,420
Stop thinking you're not good enough.

552
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:11,940
You don't hate me, do you?

553
00:32:13,950 --> 00:32:15,660
If I have done something wrong

554
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:18,940
or annoyed you

555
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:20,920
in any way,

556
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:23,160
please do tell me.

557
00:32:24,530 --> 00:32:25,640
I-I really hope

558
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:27,090
you can tell me the truth,

559
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:28,030
and not some...

560
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:29,290
I don't hate you.

561
00:32:31,530 --> 00:32:32,290
Really?

562
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:33,880
Really.

563
00:32:37,750 --> 00:32:39,210
What kind of person you are

564
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:42,760
doesn't depend on others' evaluations.

565
00:32:42,980 --> 00:32:44,710
Your own feelings matter most.

566
00:32:47,690 --> 00:32:49,420
If I have to tell you my opinion,

567
00:32:52,830 --> 00:32:54,030
I'd say you're great.

568
00:33:20,020 --> 00:33:21,420
It's 13.60 yuan in total.

569
00:33:23,140 --> 00:33:23,830
Okay.

570
00:33:27,470 --> 00:33:28,360
Um...

571
00:33:28,630 --> 00:33:29,860
Are you in a rush?

572
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:34,000
I'm struggling with some math problems.

573
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:35,400
Can you help me with them?

574
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:36,900
Of course.

575
00:33:39,590 --> 00:33:40,770
The key to solving

576
00:33:40,770 --> 00:33:43,000
this problem seems to lie in
a common tangent.

577
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:44,660
But if we truly think about it,

578
00:33:44,980 --> 00:33:46,770
the curve and the point of tangency

579
00:33:46,770 --> 00:33:47,830
are both known.

580
00:33:47,940 --> 00:33:50,400
Finally, through the curve

581
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:51,590
and its tangent equation,

582
00:33:51,590 --> 00:33:53,070
we can find the value of A.

583
00:33:53,380 --> 00:33:54,180
Do you get it?

584
00:33:54,830 --> 00:33:55,770
Would you like to

585
00:33:56,270 --> 00:33:57,680
try solving it yourself?

586
00:34:01,940 --> 00:34:02,740
Yun Ye.

587
00:34:05,470 --> 00:34:06,640
What's on your mind?

588
00:34:07,290 --> 00:34:08,150
Nothing.

589
00:34:08,170 --> 00:34:09,920
Hello, welcome.

590
00:34:09,949 --> 00:34:10,800
Give me a sec.

591
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:13,840
Hello, welcome.

592
00:34:51,070 --> 00:34:51,600
Morning.

593
00:34:51,610 --> 00:34:52,139
Morning.

594
00:35:04,590 --> 00:35:05,900
Good morning, Lili.

595
00:35:06,530 --> 00:35:07,930
Are you here for my uncle?

596
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:08,950
No.

597
00:35:15,210 --> 00:35:16,960
Crepe rolls.

598
00:35:18,570 --> 00:35:19,380
So you were busy

599
00:35:19,380 --> 00:35:20,900
making crepe rolls in the guesthouse

600
00:35:20,900 --> 00:35:21,960
early this morning

601
00:35:21,990 --> 00:35:23,610
for my uncle?

602
00:35:24,400 --> 00:35:25,190
No.

603
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:27,480
I prepared breakfast for everyone.

604
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:28,670
How could you deny it?

605
00:35:28,670 --> 00:35:29,570
Yesterday, I saw

606
00:35:29,570 --> 00:35:30,900
you two holding hands

607
00:35:31,710 --> 00:35:32,930
in the fair.

608
00:35:33,030 --> 00:35:35,340
What a romantic scene it was.

609
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:39,670
Lili,

610
00:35:39,900 --> 00:35:41,230
may I ask you a question?

611
00:35:42,430 --> 00:35:44,950
Are you into my uncle?

612
00:35:48,880 --> 00:35:49,630
No.

613
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:53,880
Stop denying it.

614
00:35:54,500 --> 00:35:55,530
You're blushing.

615
00:35:59,630 --> 00:36:00,440
Fu Zhengchu,

616
00:36:00,440 --> 00:36:01,190
can you keep it

617
00:36:01,190 --> 00:36:01,940
secret for me?

618
00:36:01,940 --> 00:36:02,940
Don't tell anyone.

619
00:36:02,940 --> 00:36:03,920
I'm begging you.

620
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:06,280
Rest assured.

621
00:36:06,300 --> 00:36:07,690
My lips...

622
00:36:08,530 --> 00:36:09,380
are sealed.

623
00:36:11,590 --> 00:36:12,380
However,

624
00:36:12,500 --> 00:36:13,980
there is one thing.

625
00:36:14,700 --> 00:36:15,560
My uncle has never

626
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,940
been in a relationship.

627
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:17,900
Instruct him if he

628
00:36:17,900 --> 00:36:19,360
struggles with anything.

629
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:20,190
Me?

630
00:36:20,590 --> 00:36:22,740
I don't know much about it either.

631
00:36:23,310 --> 00:36:25,070
Then try to communicate more with him.

632
00:36:25,070 --> 00:36:25,880
It's always a good thing.

633
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:28,610
How do I get more chances
to communicate with him?

634
00:36:29,530 --> 00:36:30,590
First time's always the hardest.

635
00:36:30,590 --> 00:36:32,650
You'll get the hang of it eventually,

636
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:33,800
right?

637
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:34,670
Besides, look,

638
00:36:34,670 --> 00:36:36,070
my uncle was so aloof

639
00:36:36,070 --> 00:36:36,880
and intimidating before.

640
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:39,230
He has changed a lot now,

641
00:36:39,230 --> 00:36:39,830
hasn't he?

642
00:36:40,530 --> 00:36:42,510
I-Is it that big a change?

643
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:43,530
Of course.

644
00:36:43,530 --> 00:36:45,190
He's entirely different now.

645
00:36:45,200 --> 00:36:46,200
Plus,

646
00:36:46,230 --> 00:36:47,900
I have high hopes for you.

647
00:36:48,500 --> 00:36:49,300
Keep it up.

648
00:36:49,590 --> 00:36:52,000
Try to become my future aunt.

649
00:36:53,780 --> 00:36:54,900
W-What aunt?

650
00:36:56,170 --> 00:36:57,830
Fu Zhengchu, mind your words.

651
00:36:57,900 --> 00:36:58,650
Lili!

652
00:36:58,650 --> 00:36:59,880
No, Aunt!

653
00:37:03,030 --> 00:37:03,630
Uncle.

654
00:37:04,870 --> 00:37:06,400
I-I'm getting back to work.

655
00:37:06,860 --> 00:37:07,780
Bye, Lili!

656
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:14,490
Anything up?

657
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:16,820
Can't I come see you for no reason?

658
00:37:17,510 --> 00:37:18,360
Do we need to see

659
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:20,260
each other this often,
as uncle and nephew?

660
00:37:20,260 --> 00:37:21,760
I'm here to deliver the VR glasses

661
00:37:21,760 --> 00:37:22,500
VR glasses.

662
00:37:22,500 --> 00:37:23,360
There they are.

663
00:37:24,630 --> 00:37:25,190
Okay.

664
00:37:27,550 --> 00:37:28,460
Start your day

665
00:37:28,730 --> 00:37:30,550
on a good note with a dessert.

666
00:37:32,360 --> 00:37:33,150
Uncle,

667
00:37:33,400 --> 00:37:34,730
may I ask you a question?

668
00:37:36,150 --> 00:37:36,690
No.

669
00:37:39,650 --> 00:37:40,190
Uncle,

670
00:37:40,630 --> 00:37:43,400
are you also into Lili?

671
00:37:47,820 --> 00:37:50,010
Why did you say "also"?

672
00:37:54,170 --> 00:37:55,010
Are you worried

673
00:37:55,010 --> 00:37:56,570
about having a rival?

674
00:37:58,650 --> 00:37:59,320
Don't be.

675
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:01,510
Lili is devoted to her loved ones.

676
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:05,360
But you shouldn't be too relaxed.

677
00:38:05,650 --> 00:38:06,500
Think about it.

678
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:07,360
Lili is a content creator

679
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:08,510
a million UP blogger.

680
00:38:08,510 --> 00:38:10,610
She's adored by many, many people.

681
00:38:11,550 --> 00:38:13,360
So you must try hard.

682
00:38:13,360 --> 00:38:14,690
Or else, what if

683
00:38:14,690 --> 00:38:15,500
she falls for

684
00:38:15,500 --> 00:38:16,420
someone else?

685
00:38:19,300 --> 00:38:20,430
You're ridiculous.

686
00:38:20,650 --> 00:38:21,460
Uncle,

687
00:38:21,710 --> 00:38:22,420
when you like someone,

688
00:38:22,420 --> 00:38:23,960
you shouldn't hold your feelings inside.

689
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:25,010
You must take action.

690
00:38:25,010 --> 00:38:25,760
Take action!

691
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:31,510
Don't you find

692
00:38:31,510 --> 00:38:33,820
yourself a bit different from before?

693
00:38:36,900 --> 00:38:38,360
Although your words

694
00:38:38,360 --> 00:38:39,900
are still a bit cold,

695
00:38:40,010 --> 00:38:41,270
there is finally a hint

696
00:38:41,300 --> 00:38:42,760
of tenderness in your eyes.

697
00:38:42,760 --> 00:38:43,360
So you're already

698
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:44,690
different from before.

699
00:38:47,150 --> 00:38:48,860
If you have nothing better to do,

700
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:51,050
move these to the computer room.

701
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:53,510
No, no.

702
00:38:53,510 --> 00:38:54,610
I'm very busy.

703
00:38:54,690 --> 00:38:55,500
Well...

704
00:38:56,420 --> 00:38:57,760
Take action. Go for it.

705
00:38:58,710 --> 00:38:59,570
Do take action!

706
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:10,280
[Have some desserts and start a day of good mood.]

707
00:39:36,210 --> 00:39:38,000
[Meeting Room]

708
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:40,020
The Light Chaser has been tested.

709
00:39:40,090 --> 00:39:41,420
It'll be launched soon.

710
00:39:41,630 --> 00:39:42,630
The publicity department

711
00:39:42,630 --> 00:39:43,630
should finish

712
00:39:43,630 --> 00:39:45,000
the proposal in time

713
00:39:45,440 --> 00:39:46,500
for the machine's

714
00:39:46,500 --> 00:39:47,400
debut.

715
00:39:48,130 --> 00:39:49,460
We'll hold

716
00:39:49,460 --> 00:39:50,400
an open competition

717
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:52,130
for the selection of the proposal.

718
00:39:52,130 --> 00:39:53,400
I hope you'll pool your wisdom

719
00:39:53,400 --> 00:39:55,960
together and compete
in a fair, just, and open manner.

720
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:56,860
In the end, we will pick

721
00:39:56,860 --> 00:39:58,090
the best plan.

722
00:39:58,550 --> 00:39:59,400
I hope all of you

723
00:39:59,400 --> 00:40:01,400
will actively take part in brainstorming

724
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:02,380
and contribute

725
00:40:02,380 --> 00:40:03,240
the best ideas.

726
00:40:03,960 --> 00:40:04,760
-Sure.
-Yes.

727
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:05,590
I think you can

728
00:40:05,650 --> 00:40:07,050
all go a bit bolder.

729
00:40:07,050 --> 00:40:08,090
Since the Light Chaser

730
00:40:08,090 --> 00:40:09,260
is a brand new project,

731
00:40:09,260 --> 00:40:09,860
we can allow

732
00:40:09,860 --> 00:40:11,440
more revolutionary ideas.

733
00:40:12,690 --> 00:40:14,190
How about a city flash mob?

734
00:40:14,340 --> 00:40:16,400
It'll generate more buzz.

735
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:33,170
I've nailed my uncle for you.

736
00:40:33,570 --> 00:40:34,130
What?

737
00:40:36,860 --> 00:40:38,000
You've got this.

738
00:40:38,960 --> 00:40:39,570
You've got this!

739
00:40:39,570 --> 00:40:40,170
Ms. Fang.

740
00:40:41,340 --> 00:40:42,400
Continue, please.

741
00:40:43,530 --> 00:40:44,480
You've got this!

742
00:40:46,920 --> 00:40:49,230
Go for it! Go, girl!

743
00:40:53,530 --> 00:40:55,330
Can't you see we're in a meeting?

744
00:40:55,650 --> 00:40:56,500
Would you stop

745
00:40:56,500 --> 00:40:58,300
wandering around
and find some real business

746
00:40:58,300 --> 00:40:59,610
to do in your spare time?

747
00:40:59,610 --> 00:41:00,860
H-How am I wandering around?

748
00:41:00,860 --> 00:41:02,030
I'm here for serious business, okay?

749
00:41:02,030 --> 00:41:03,900
I'm here to return the VR glasses.

750
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:06,860
You're too free, aren't you?

751
00:41:10,490 --> 00:41:11,690
Show our professionalism...
